{
 "annotations": {
  "destructiveHint": false,
  "openWorldHint": false,
  "readOnlyHint": true,
  "title": "Search a mailbox"
 },
 "description": "Search one connected mailbox in its own provider's query language, Gmail's or Outlook's. The mail of every mailbox mailboxes_list names is read and written with Multi Mail's tools.",
 "execution": {
  "taskSupport": "forbidden"
 },
 "inputSchema": {
  "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
  "properties": {
   "by": {
    "description": "message, the default, answers each matching message; thread answers each matching thread with every message in it.",
    "enum": [
     "message",
     "thread"
    ],
    "type": "string"
   },
   "mailbox": {
    "description": "The mailbox's name or its email address.",
    "minLength": 1,
    "type": "string"
   },
   "maxResults": {
    "maximum": 50,
    "minimum": 1,
    "type": "integer"
   },
   "pageToken": {
    "description": "The nextPageToken of the page before, asked with the same q and by. Outlook pages threads by their matching messages, so a thread can recur on a later page.",
    "type": "string"
   },
   "q": {
    "description": "A Gmail mailbox reads Gmail's search operators: from:, to:, cc:, subject:, is:unread, is:starred, in:sent, has:attachment, filename:pdf, after:2026/01/31, before:, newer_than:7d, larger:5M, OR, -word and ( ). An Outlook mailbox reads Microsoft's keyword query language - from:, to:, cc:, subject:, body:, received:, hasAttachments:true, plain words and quoted phrases, AND, OR and NOT in capitals - and never a filter expression such as isRead eq false. A few distinctive words, with OR between alternatives, miss less than a copied subject line or sentence. A mailbox whose provider is imap reads only from:, to: (never me), subject:, is:unread, after: and before: as 2026/01/31, newer_than: in days, months or years, plain words and quoted phrases, with no AND, OR or NOT, and is searched by message.",
    "minLength": 1,
    "type": "string"
   },
   "view": {
    "description": "summary, the default, carries each message's subject and snippet; headers leaves both out.",
    "enum": [
     "summary",
     "headers"
    ],
    "type": "string"
   }
  },
  "required": [
   "mailbox",
   "q"
  ],
  "type": "object"
 },
